<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=galen">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Medicine and health</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">129–c. 216 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galen was a Greek physician of the second century CE whose writings dominated medicine for centuries. His works were translated into Arabic during the translation movement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, preserving them and shaping medical science in the Islamic world and later in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galen.jpg" alt="Galen" width="254" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Paul Busch (engraver) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galenus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>162 CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Rome</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/galen">Galen</a> · <a href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></dd></div></dl><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/hippocratic-corpus">Hippocratic medicine<span>5th century BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bimaristan">Hospital (bimaristan)<span>805</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/the-canon-of-medicine">The Canon of Medicine<span>1025</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/de-humani-corporis-fabrica">Modern anatomy<span>1543</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=galen">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
